        <h2>Summary / Description</h2>
        <div class="description">
          The graph provides an overview of what was known in 1993 of the effects of space flight (0g space and 1g space), hypergravity (10g centrifuge), simulated low-g (0.02g clinostat), and cosmic radiation (1g stratospheric balloon) on mitogenic activation of T-lymphocytes by Con A.  The experiments were conducted either with resuspended (-MC) or microcarrier (MC)-attaced cells (+MC).  The bars give the percent of activation (measured on day 3 after exposure to Con A at 37 degrees Celsius as counts per minute of tritiated thymidine incorporated into DNA) with respect of the relative control (taken as 100%) on the ground (1g ground) without MC beads.  Because the number of independent experiments shown in the diagram varies from 1 to 20, standard errors are not given in the graph.<P>In Cogoli A.  The effect of hypogravity and hypergravity on cells of the immune system.  <I>J. Leukocyte Biology</I>, 1993, 54, 259-268.<END>
        </div>

